    "summary_short": "When a young girl's suppressed childhood trauma resurfaces, former police officer Vetri Kondan steps up to protect her and guide her toward joining the military. However, her deep-seated fears stem from a powerful global extremist seeking total control over democratic institutions. Drawn back into action, Vetri must wage a high-stakes battle that transcends personal vengeance to protect both his ward and the nation.",
    "summary_long": "Vetri Kondan, a fearless former police officer, assumes guardianship of Viji, the daughter of his late friend. Determined to help her overcome a severe childhood trauma and achieve her dream of enlisting in the army, Vetri works tirelessly to rebuild her confidence. Their quiet lives are upended when Viji's hidden past connects back to Phoenix, a power-hungry international extremist plotting to incite chaos and subvert democratic governance. Realizing that the threat extends far beyond his immediate family, Vetri re-enters the fray to dismantle Phoenix's treacherous web. Across intense ideological and physical clashes, Vetri inspires ordinary citizens while protecting Viji from ongoing danger. Ultimately, Vetri helps Viji conquer her silent fear while mounting a decisive resistance against tyrannical authority, proving that true power belongs to the people.",
    "synopsis": "Jana Nayagan follows Vetri Kondan, a dedicated former police officer who takes custody of his deceased friend's daughter, Viji. As Vetri tries to heal Viji's severe childhood trauma and support her ambitions to join the Indian Army, her past re-emerges through a powerful global extremist named Phoenix. Operating on greed and total control, Phoenix poses a direct threat to national security and democratic freedom. Vetri is forced back into action to defend his ward and confront the systemic corrupt power structure, turning a personal mission of protection into a nationwide fight for justice.",
